======================================================================
  CYCLE SPACE EXTENSIONS: CONNECTING EVERYTHING
======================================================================

======================================================================
  1. FORBIDDEN H=7 IN CYCLE SPACE
======================================================================

  H=7 requires 2*a1 + 4*a2 + ... = 6
  Solutions: (a1=3, a2=0) or (a1=1, a2=1)

  (a1=3, a2=0): 3 cycles, all pairwise conflicting
    => all share a common vertex (THM-029)
    => common vertex has 2 in-arcs from cycle partners
    => creates a 5-cycle => alpha_1 >= 4. CONTRADICTION.

  (a1=1, a2=1): 1 cycle + 1 disjoint pair
    => a disjoint pair needs >=2 cycles, but a1=1. CONTRADICTION.

  H=7 IS FORBIDDEN BECAUSE NO VALID CYCLE SPACE CONFIGURATION EXISTS.
  The impossibility is PURELY in the cycle space (even graph component).
  Scores are irrelevant -- no score sequence can produce H=7.

